			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T18:49:08Z",
			"File": [
				"⡟⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1858,
				300
			],
			"Message": "docs(Mountain): Add missing rustdoc comments and strip meta-instructional text\n\nAdd `///` doc comments to every public type alias, free function, and struct in the Mountain codebase that was previously undocumented. Strip \"This struct/function...\" meta-instructional preamble from existing doc comments, remove empty `///` separator lines, and delete redundant `# Arguments` / `# Returns` section markers that add no value.\n\nKey changes:\n- Added doc stubs to 400+ `pub type`, `pub fn`, `pub struct`, and `pub enum` items across Air, ApplicationState, Cache, Command, Environment, Error, ExtensionManagement, FileSystem, IPC, ProcessManagement, RPC, RunTime, Telemetry, Track, Update, Vine, and Workspace modules\n- Rewrote `/// This struct/function/enum...` patterns into direct descriptions (`/// Configuration state for tree views` not `/// This struct represents...`)\n- Removed all bare `///` empty doc-comment lines\n- Collapsed spaced-out `# Arguments` / `# Returns` blocks to compact `## Parameters` / `## Returns` style in CocoonStart.rs, VineStart.rs, CocoonService/mod.rs, Initialize.rs, and MountainVinegRPCService.rs\n- Updated `fix_rustdocs.py` and `rewrite_docs.py` automation scripts with improved false-positive detection and smarter PascalCase-to-description generation",
			"SHA": "a995d3b0abbea170a5e6e53f751cc22ed843539c"
